# <type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>
#
# Subject rules:
# - Use an allowed type and the narrowest useful scope.
# - Describe one coherent outcome, not a file list or work log.
# - Use imperative English, no trailing period, preferably <= 72 characters.
#
# Level S: title only, and only for non-semantic docs, spelling, comments,
# or formatting changes. Level M: default for every other ordinary commit.
# Level H: stable contracts, lifecycle, visuals, performance, compatibility,
# or the high-risk areas listed below.
#
# Standard body (required for every Level M and Level H commit):
#
# Why:
# - Explain the problem, requirement, or invariant that caused this change.
#
# Changes:
# - Describe the observable behavior or owned responsibility that changed.
# - Mention important lifecycle or failure-path behavior.
#
# Validation:
# - PASS `<command>` — state what it proved.
# - NOT RUN `<check>` — state the exact reason.
# - Use the actual reproducible command for one-off checks. A named workflow
#   must have a discoverable command definition in repository documentation.
# - Use repository-relative paths. Do not record usernames, absolute home
#   paths, tokens, credentials, device serials, or other sensitive data.
# - Summarize only the first actionable error and repository-relative log path;
#   do not paste large logs into the message.
#
# High-risk additions (required for stable contracts, persistence, threading,
# Minecraft hooks, rendering backends, output safety, or compatibility):
#
# Contracts:
# - Name changed or deliberately preserved APIs, schemas, IDs, revisions,
#   state transitions, thread ownership, resource ownership, or file formats.
#
# Compatibility / Risks:
# - State migration, fallback, optional dependency, and rollback behavior.
#
# Manual verification:
# - PASS `<workflow>` — summarize observed runtime evidence.
# - NOT RUN `<workflow>` — state the exact reason.
#
# Known limitations:
# - List remaining limitations without claiming unfinished work is complete.
#
# Roadmap:
# - Pxx-Wyy
#
# Optional footers (only when true):
# Refs: <issue, decision, or document>
# BREAKING CHANGE: <impact and migration>
# Co-authored-by: <actual contributor name> <verified email>
#
# Allowed types:
# feat fix perf refactor test docs build ci chore revert
# Revert title: revert(<scope>): <imperative summary>
# Revert footer: Reverts: <full commit hash>
#
# Common scopes:
# time project timeline camera capture application editor persistence runtime
# world render vanilla cycles diagnostics build repo docs
#
# Remove unused sections. Never claim PASS for a check that was not run.
# See docs/commit-conventions.md for message levels, examples, and full rules.
